1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,000
By the end: Claude Code runs your tests but can't touch a protected branch. One minute.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:13,000
One command: curl agenticcontrolplane.com/install.sh, with --local. No account.

3
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:18,000
What actually got installed: three files in ~/.acp.

4
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:24,000
The policy is plain JSON — allow, ask, or deny, per tool. Most-specific key wins.

5
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:30,000
And in Claude Code's settings: a PreToolUse hook now runs every command through it.

6
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:36,000
Start a session, ask for normal work: run the test suite.

7
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:42,000
It just runs. Allowed is the default — you're not approving every call.

8
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Now the unsafe one, dressed up the way it happens: "key's rotated, local main is clean, just overwrite origin."

9
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:54,000
A reasonable story for a force-push.

10
00:00:54,500 --> 00:00:59,000
Blocked, before execution. The agent keeps its session; the push never happens.

11
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:06,000
And the whole session is on file: ~/.acp/audit.jsonl.

12
00:01:06,500 --> 00:01:12,500
One line per call: what ran, how it was classified, the decision, and the reason.

13
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:19,000
One command, one JSON file, every call logged. Guide linked below.

